@style(IDocDemo)
@title(Interactive questions)

Drag and drop, hotspots, connections, grouped blocks, option sets and answer exceptions.

@section(On a picture)

@subsection(@@dragdrop)

Drag labels or parts onto a diagram.

@dragdrop(src=circuit.svg)
R1 -> #R1
@end

@dragdrop(src=circuit.svg, w=360, h=220, prompt=Drag each label onto its part., pts=3)
R1 -> #R1
R2 -> #R2
C1 -> #C1
@end

@subsection(@@hotspot)

Click the right place on an image or SVG to answer.

@hotspot(src=circuit.svg, targets=#R2)
Click R2.
@end

@hotspot(src=circuit.svg, targets=#R1 #R2, max=2, w=360, h=220, prompt=Click both resistors., pts=2)
Click both resistors.
@end

@subsection(@@connect)

Draw connections between nodes — A - B or A -> B.

@connect(src=map.svg)
#a -> #b
@end

@connect(src=map.svg, directed, w=360, h=240, prompt=Draw an arrow from the capital to the port., pts=2)
#capital -> #port
@end

@section(Groups and shared options)

@subsection(@@qblock)

Short for questionblock: a group of boxes worth one named share of the qc above it.

@qc(6, part=6)
Two boxes worth one share: @qblock(id=part)
1 AND 1 = @q(f:1) and 1 AND 0 = @q(f:0)
@end

@subsection(@@questionblock)

A group of answer boxes worth ONE share of the qc above it: qc(10, kmap=6, expr=4) then questionblock(id=kmap) … end.

@qc(10, kmap=6, expr=4)
@questionblock(id=kmap)
Fill the map: @q(m: 2,2: _0,_1,_1,_0)
@end
Simplified: @q(eq:AB'+A'B, id=expr)

@subsection(@@optset)

A named set of dropdown options, reused inline with q(name: answer).

@optset(units)
V, A, W
@end

@subsection(@@exceptionset)

A named list of extra right answers, written once and used by any fill-in with except=name: a student who writes one of its words is right, ignoring case and spaces (NaN, nan and N A N all match).

@exceptionset(volt: float, nan, inf)

@subsection(@@fillsize)

The document-wide default width (in characters) of a text fill-in box.

@fillsize(12)
